      "reason_summary": "Both Historian A and B agree on the core historical identity: 大將軍 refers to 王敦 (Wang Dun), who held the title of Grand General. The main text confirms this: 謝鯤爲豫章太守從大將軍下至石頭, followed by 敦謂鯤曰, showing 大將軍 and 敦 are the same person. The Liu annotation (sfh1-ev-10-guizhen-012-liu-annotation-002) explicitly mentions 王敦. Historian B's additional relations are problematic: it adds a \"related_person\" relation to 謝鯤 (who is the subject accompanying 大將軍, not a relation target of the office-title reference itself), and it splits the same_person relation into two targets (敦 and 王敦) which are the same person, creating redundant/duplicate relation entries. Historian A's single same_person relation to 王敦 is cleaner and historically accurate. The discourse fields in A (antecedent_hint 王敦, no speaker_hint) are appropriate for an office-title reference in narrative text; B's speaker_hint 敘述者 is unnecessary metadata. Historian A's record is the more precise and defensible hypothesis.",
